@startuml 08a_seq_find_view
' Sequence diagram 1 — Find a place and view its accessibility (v0.4, 2026-11-01)
' Changes from v0.3: the same flow runs on the public website (Next.js pages), which calls the
' server code directly instead of /api; no markers for unrated places; shared links open the website.
' Stack: Expo app with MapLibre · Next.js backend (route handlers) · D1 · R2 · OpenStreetMap tiles
!include _seq.iuml
title 1 · Find a place and view its accessibility

actor "Map user\n(no account needed)" as U
participant "Mobile app\nor website" as App
box "Backend · Next.js on Cloudflare" #FAFAFA
  participant "API route\n+ requireRole()" as API
  database "D1" as DB
end box
participant "R2\n(photos)" as R2
participant "Map tile\nprovider" as Tiles

== Open the map ==
U -> App : open app
App -> Tiles : get map tiles
Tiles --> App : tiles (OpenStreetMap)
App -> API : GET /api/places
note right of API : public route:\nno sign-in needed
API -> DB : all visible places:\nid, coordinates, category,\ncurrent level (or unrated),\nno-parking flag
DB --> API : rows
API --> App : place list
App -> App : cache list, draw colored\nmarkers + clusters for rated places\n(unrated: base-map labels only)

== Search ==
U -> App : type "spital"
App -> API : GET /api/search?q=spital
API -> DB : full-text search (FTS5):\nprefix match, ignores diacritics
DB --> API : matching places
API --> App : results (rated + unrated)
App --> U : result list

== View a place ==
U -> App : tap a place
App -> API : GET /api/places/{id}
API -> DB : place + CURRENT assessment:\nlevel, answer per criterion,\nlast verified, photo keys
DB --> API : rows
API -> API : make short-lived\nsigned photo links
API --> App : place details
App -> R2 : load photos (signed links)
R2 --> App : photos
App --> U : level, each criterion,\nphotos, last verified

note over App, API
  Only approved data is ever returned.
  The website runs the same steps, but its pages
  call the server code directly instead of /api.
  A shared place link opens the place on the website.
  A place with no published rating shows
  "Not yet rated" with an "Assess this place" button.
end note

opt user wants to go there
  U -> App : tap "Directions"
  App -> App : open phone's maps app\nwith the coordinates
end
@enduml
